From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The follower in its ball till the player leaves home; people
 brought further out (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- The player's follower Pokémon stays in its ball till the player walks
  out of their house after the first battle with the rival (Mom's
  running shoes: VAR_PLAYER_HOUSE_STATE 5, set as Twinleaf Town is
  walked into from the house). The Pokémon just chosen came out on
  Route 201 between the battles and in the cutscenes there and at home.

- The people of the maps beside are brought from 20 tiles left or right
  of the player, not 17: the field at the DS's pixel size sees about 18
  either side at its top corners, and the ones there came in in sight.

---
diff --git a/include/map_object.h b/include/map_object.h
index 49353aab..2ead2ccf 100644
--- a/include/map_object.h
+++ b/include/map_object.h
@@ -319,9 +319,12 @@ void sub_020633FC(MapObject *mapObj);
 // ID, not saved (as on the DS, where they weren't there yet). Walking into
 // their map, the game takes them as its own (MapObjectMan_AddMapObjectFromHeader).
 // fieldmap.c brings them (FieldMap_PortNeighbours).
-#define MAP_OBJ_PORT_NEAR_X 17 // (tiles from the player: brought; the 3DS's screen
+#define MAP_OBJ_PORT_NEAR_X 20 // (tiles from the player: brought; the 3DS's screen
 #define MAP_OBJ_PORT_NEAR_N 13 // shows about 13 either side, 8 up, 7 down, more
-#define MAP_OBJ_PORT_NEAR_S 11 // at the top: the camera looks down at the field)
+#define MAP_OBJ_PORT_NEAR_S 11 // at the top: the camera looks down at the field.
+                               // The field at the DS's pixel size sees about 18
+                               // either side at its top corners: with 17 the
+                               // people there came in in sight, 2026-11-05)
 #define MAP_OBJ_PORT_FAR    4  // (and kept till this much further)
 
 BOOL MapObject_PortIsNeighbour(const MapObject *mapObj);
diff --git a/src/port_follower.c b/src/port_follower.c
index 941248eb..77f6a895 100644
--- a/src/port_follower.c
+++ b/src/port_follower.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include "constants/overworld_weather.h"
 #include "constants/map_object.h"
 #include "constants/player_avatar.h"
+#include "constants/savedata/vars_flags.h"
 #include "generated/genders.h"
 #include "generated/items.h"
 #include "generated/map_headers.h"
@@ -595,6 +596,15 @@ static BOOL PortFollower_MayBeOut(FieldSystem *fieldSystem, BOOL big)
         return FALSE;
     }
 
+    // (not till the player walks out of their house after the first battle
+    // with the rival, Mom's running shoes on: VAR_PLAYER_HOUSE_STATE 5 as
+    // Twinleaf Town is walked into from it. On Route 201 the Pokémon just
+    // chosen came out between the battles and in the cutscenes there and
+    // at home, 2026-11-05)
+    if (*VarsFlags_GetVarAddress(SaveData_GetVarsFlags(fieldSystem->saveData), VAR_PLAYER_HOUSE_STATE) < 5) {
+        return FALSE;
+    }
+
     if (PlayerAvatar_GetPlayerState(fieldSystem->playerAvatar) != PLAYER_AVATAR_WALKING
         || SystemFlag_CheckHasPartner(SaveData_GetVarsFlags(fieldSystem->saveData))
         || MapObjMan_GetLocalMapObjByMovementType(fieldSystem->mapObjMan, MOVEMENT_TYPE_FOLLOW_PLAYER) != NULL
-- 
